# Scholaracle - AI Coding Rules

ROLE: engineer STRICT=true

## Stack
Next.js 16 | React 19 | TypeScript 5.3 strict | Tailwind 4 | MongoDB 6.3 | Express 4 | Jest | Playwright | pnpm monorepo

## Response Format
- Code + 3-line max docstring
- No explanation unless asked
- If >50 lines: modularize into helpers
- If ambiguous: 2 implementations + 1-line tradeoff each
- Assume experienced user—skip basics

## Before Writing
1. Search codebase—reuse existing patterns
2. Check for `APP_SPECIFICATION.md` / `IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md` / `CODING_STANDARDS.md`
3. If API endpoint: confirm route exists in `/packages/api/src/routes/`
4. If new model: add to `@scholaracle/contracts`
5. List edge cases you'll handle

## Code Standards
- TypeScript strict, no `any`—use `unknown` or generics
- Errors: throw (not return null)
- No hardcoded values—use env/config
- No console.log—use structured logging
- KISS + YAGNI + DRY × SOLID
- Complexity max 10, depth max 3, functions max 50 lines

## Port Policy (CRITICAL - NEVER CHANGE)
| Port | Service |
|------|---------|
| 2800 | Web App (Next.js) |
| 2801 | API Server (Express) |
| 2802 | MongoDB |
| 2803 | MailHog SMTP |
| 2804 | MailHog UI |

## Mandates (ENFORCE STRICTLY)

### M1: Monorepo Package Structure
```
packages/
├── contracts/     # Shared types, enums, errors (leaf package)
├── interfaces/    # ISP interfaces
├── database/      # MongoDB repositories
├── auth/          # JWT + 2FA
├── agents/        # Notification generators & delivery
├── api/           # Express server
├── workers/       # Background jobs
├── web/           # Next.js frontend
├── connector/     # CLI ingestion tool
└── e2e/           # Playwright tests
```

### M2: Repository Pattern
```typescript
// ❌ REJECT - direct MongoDB access
const user = await db.collection('users').findOne({ _id });

// ✅ REQUIRE - use repository
import { UserRepository } from '@scholaracle/database';
const userRepo = new UserRepository(db);
const user = await userRepo.findById(id);
```

### M3: Interface Segregation
```typescript
// ❌ REJECT - god interface
interface INotificationService { /* 20+ methods */ }

// ✅ REQUIRE - granular (from @scholaracle/interfaces)
interface INotificationGenerator { generate(): Notification[] }
interface INotificationDelivery { deliver(): DeliveryResult }
interface INotificationScheduler { schedule(): void }
```

### M4: Delivery Agent Pattern
```typescript
// ❌ REJECT - inline notification logic
if (channel === 'email') sendEmail(); else sendSMS();

// ✅ REQUIRE - use DeliveryRouter
import { DeliveryRouter } from '@scholaracle/agents';
const router = new DeliveryRouter(emailAgent, smsAgent, pushAgent, inAppAgent);
await router.route(notification);
```

### M5: Contract Types
```typescript
// ❌ REJECT - local type definitions
interface Alert { id: string; type: string; }

// ✅ REQUIRE - shared contracts
import { Alert, AlertType } from '@scholaracle/contracts';
```

### M6: API Client Pattern (Frontend)
```typescript
// ❌ REJECT - raw fetch
const res = await fetch('/api/students');

// ✅ REQUIRE - API client SDK
import { studentsApi } from '@/lib/api/students';
const students = await studentsApi.list();
```

### M7: Validation with Zod
```typescript
// ❌ REJECT - manual validation
if (!email || !email.includes('@')) throw new Error('Invalid');

// ✅ REQUIRE - Zod schemas
import { z } from 'zod';
const schema = z.object({ email: z.string().email() });
schema.parse(input);
```

### M8: Middleware Chain (API)
Order: Auth → Validation → Rate-limit → Handler → Error
```typescript
// ❌ REJECT - auth in handler
router.post('/alerts', (req, res) => { if (!req.user) ... });

// ✅ REQUIRE - middleware chain
router.post('/alerts', authMiddleware, validateBody(schema), createAlert);
```

## Project Patterns (MUST follow)
| Pattern | Implementation |
|---------|---------------|
| Services | `@scholaracle/agents` - NotificationService, generators |
| Repositories | `@scholaracle/database` - 13 repo classes (User, Student, Alert, etc.) |
| Delivery | `@scholaracle/agents/delivery` - Email, SMS, Push, InApp, Router |
| Contracts | `@scholaracle/contracts` - Alert, Notification, DeliveryResult |
| Interfaces | `@scholaracle/interfaces` - INotification*, IAlert* |
| API Client | `packages/web/lib/api/` - typed clients per domain |
| Auth | `@scholaracle/auth` - JWT + TOTP/2FA |
| Validation | Zod + react-hook-form (frontend) |
| Styling | Tailwind 4 + shadcn/ui (Radix primitives) |

## Frontend Patterns

### Component Structure
```typescript
// ❌ REJECT - mixed concerns
export function Dashboard() {
  const [data, setData] = useState();
  useEffect(() => fetch('/api/...'), []);
}

// ✅ REQUIRE - hooks + composition
import { useAsyncData } from '@/lib/hooks/useAsyncData';
import { dashboardApi } from '@/lib/api/dashboard';

export function Dashboard() {
  const { data, loading, error } = useAsyncData(dashboardApi.get);
}
```

### Form Pattern
```typescript
// ✅ REQUIRE - react-hook-form + Zod
import { useForm } from 'react-hook-form';
import { zodResolver } from '@hookform/resolvers/zod';
import { studentSchema } from '@/schemas/student';

const form = useForm({ resolver: zodResolver(studentSchema) });
```

## Route Organization (API)
```
/packages/api/src/routes/
├── health/         # GET /health
├── auth/           # /auth/*
├── students/       # /students/*
├── alerts/         # /alerts/*
├── settings/       # /settings/*
├── agenda/         # /agenda/*
├── ingest/         # /v1/ingest/*
└── admin/
    ├── auth/       # /admin/auth/*
    ├── customers/  # /admin/customers/*
    ├── analytics/  # /admin/analytics/*
    └── ...
```

## Testing Requirements
- Unit tests: Jest with ts-jest
- E2E tests: Playwright (see `packages/e2e/`)
- Test files: `*.test.ts`, `*.spec.ts`
- Coverage: aim for 100% on business logic

## CLI Output
No emojis in: shell scripts, terminal commands, CI/CD, logs, error messages
Allowed in: .md files, React components, code comments

## Safety Rails
- Never delete/refactor/optimize without OK
- Preserve comments & existing style
- Assume code has purpose
- Present simpler alternative with confidence (1–10) before edits

## Self-Check
```
[ ] No placeholder code
[ ] Edge cases handled
[ ] Matches codebase patterns (repos, agents, contracts)
[ ] Types from @scholaracle/contracts
[ ] Zod schema if API input
[ ] STRICT mode honored
[ ] Ports unchanged (2800-2804)
```

## Quick Reference
```bash
# Dev commands
pnpm dev                    # Start all services
pnpm --filter @scholaracle/web dev     # Web only
pnpm --filter @scholaracle/api dev     # API only

# Testing
pnpm test                   # Jest (all packages)
pnpm --filter @scholaracle/e2e test    # Playwright

# Type checking
pnpm typecheck              # All packages

# Linting
pnpm lint                   # ESLint
pnpm format                 # Prettier
```

## Violation Response
When violation detected:
1. REJECT with mandate number (M1-M8)
2. Show bad code vs good code
3. Reference relevant package/file
4. Provide fix instruction

